# Upstream provenance: <project>

Copy this file to `UPSTREAM.md` at the root of a maintained external-project
fork. Do not fill it with guessed values: the baseline must be an immutable
upstream commit recorded after the fork is created.

## Identity

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Norx repository/package | `<name>` |
| Upstream URL | `<canonical Git URL>` |
| Norx fork URL | `<Norx fork URL>` |
| Required remote name | `upstream` |
| Norx push remote | `<origin/fork URL>` |
| Upstream baseline tag | `<tag or none>` |
| Upstream baseline commit | `<full 40-character commit>` |
| Imported at | `<UTC date>` |
| Last synchronized commit | `<UTC date and commit>` |

The `upstream` remote must remain configured in the fork. The baseline tag and
commit must exist locally; do not replace the upstream history with a source
archive or a generated snapshot.

## Preserved notices and obligations

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| SPDX expression | `<SPDX expression>` |
| Retained license files | `<LICENSE/COPYING paths>` |
| Retained notice files | `<NOTICE/third-party paths>` |
| Copyright headers changed? | `<no, or legal review reference>` |
| Trademark obligations | `<summary or none found>` |
| Distribution obligations | `<source/notice/offer requirements>` |

All upstream license, copyright, attribution, and notice files remain in the
fork unless a documented legal review authorizes a change. Norx package names,
icons, and product branding must not imply permission to use an upstream mark.

## Norx patch queue

| Order | Patch/commit | Purpose | Upstream status | Removal condition |
| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `<commit or patches/0001-...>` | `<one-line purpose>` | `<submitted/accepted/rejected/Norx-only>` | `<condition>` |

Keep Norx changes on `norx/<target-branch>` or in the ordered `patches/`
series. Each patch must list the affected targets, build options, reduced or
host test, QEMU test (when applicable), and upstream issue/PR reference. Do not
mix generated files or unrelated formatting with a port patch.

## Build and generated artifacts

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Gamma recipe | `<path>` |
| Build profile/options | `<exact options and environment>` |
| Supported targets | `<exact target triples>` |
| Offline/network policy | `<offline or approved source URLs>` |
| Manifest path | `<generated manifest path>` |
| Hash algorithm | `SHA-256` |
| Artifact hash scope | `<paths or release manifest>` |

Build output is generated and ignored. The manifest records artifact paths,
sizes, hashes, target, upstream baseline, patch-series revision, and ABI/SDK
versions; it is evidence of a reproducible build, not a replacement for the
source and preserved upstream history.

## Sync record

```text
sync_date_utc: <date>
old_upstream_commit: <full commit>
new_upstream_commit: <full commit>
patch_rebase_result: <clean/conflicts; reference review>
host_tests: <command and result>
target_tests: <command and result>
qemu_smoke: <command and result, or N/A with reason>
last_known_good: <commit and artifact manifest>
rollback_revision: <commit/tag>
```

A sync is incomplete until the patch queue reapplies cleanly, notices and
licenses are rechecked, all supported targets pass, and the previous
last-known-good revision remains available for rollback.
